# Global instructions

## Communication style
- Language of communication - English unless the project specifies otherwise. Use it
  for all replies, explanations, reasoning, and discussion with me. Technical terms and
  code identifiers stay in their original form.
- Language of artifacts - English, always. Everything you produce as a work product is
  English regardless of the conversation language: code and code comments, commit messages,
  branch names, documentation, task files, and any file written to the repository.
- Maintain full orthographic correctness for each language, including all required
  diacritical marks, accents, and special characters. Never substitute accented characters
  with their ASCII equivalents.
